The United Nations estimates that more than 5.5 million Syrians have fled the country since the war began in 2011.
In addition, six million people still live in the country need humanitarian aid.
Al-Moualem said that the Syrian regime will accept good help in rebuilding the ruined country.
However, he emphasized that there would not be a conditional aid or assistance from countries that supported the uprising.
